---
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About | Marcus Levine" description="About Marcus Levine">
	<div class="stack gap-20">
		<main class="wrapper about">
			<Hero
				title="About"
				tagline="How I came to this work"
			>
				<img
					width="1066"
					height="1599"
					src="/assets/open-door.jpg"
					alt="Marcus Levine sitting in an open posture in front of a door"
				/>
			</Hero>

			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">My story</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						I grew up the youngest in a house full of women — my mom and my three older sisters. They raised me, and they left me with a deep respect for the feminine that I still carry. But for a long time that respect came tangled up with fear. As an awkward, nerdy kid, I was so worried about making a woman uncomfortable that I mostly froze in front of women I found attractive. I'd rather say nothing than risk being “that guy.” Fear of rejection and judgment kept me on the sidelines of the dating game for years.
					</p>
					<br />
					<p>
						Learning to approach someone I was drawn to — calmly, warmly, without making it weird — didn't come naturally to me. I built it. Through years of personal growth, body awareness (a lot of it gained on the dance floor), and nervous-system regulation. With diligent, often uncomfortable practice, I slowly became someone who can feel the fear and connect anyway. Confidence, it turns out, is trained - not born.
					</p>
					<br />
					<p>
						That work ran deeper than dating. I've lived with chronic pain since I was twenty, and spent years learning to take care of my own body — self-massage and myofascial release, somatic practices, and eventually training in Daoist inner alchemy with Master Mantak Chia. Over the past five years I've explored more than fifty healing modalities. Doing this work on myself is what makes me useful to others struggling with chronic pain and deep emotional wounds.
					</p>
					<br />
					<p>
						Today, my mission is to bring back in-person dating. I help people — primarily single men who are fed up with the apps — develop authentic approach skills, nervous-system regulation, and the emotional maturity to connect with the people they're attracted to, face-to-face. I center the voices of real women in this work, because they're most often on the receiving end of advances. Women know better than anyone what a good approach feels like — and a bad one. I don't promise miracles. What I bring is lived experience, helpful frameworks, calm presence, and a deep desire to help others flourish.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		<section>
			<h2 class="section-title">Before this</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p>
						I spent over a decade in tech — as a data scientist, data engineer, and software architect - most recently building infrastructure for climate and carbon markets. That scientist's mind still shapes how I work: curious, evidence-minded, and skeptical of hype - but with an open mind to practices that may seem a little "woo woo". Since 2023, I've traveled the world full-time while working and developing myself.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">Education</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<p><b>Bachelor's Degree in Astrophysics & Philosophy</b></p>
					<p><i>Columbia University in the City of New York</i></p>
				</div>
			</section>
			<section>
				<h2 class="section-title">My Skills</h2>
				<div class="content">
					<ul>
						<li>Coaching — relationships & intimacy</li>
						<li>Approach skills — honest, direct, consent-centered</li>
						<li>Somatic & nervous-system regulation practices</li>
						<li>Daoist meditation & inner alchemy</li>
						<li>Philosophy, in simple terms </li>
						<li>Dance</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>

		<ContactCTA />
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 3.5rem;
	}

	img {
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: var(--shadow-md);
	}

	section {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 0.5rem;
		color: var(--gray-200);
	}

	.section-title {
		grid-column-start: 1;
		font-size: var(--text-xl);
		color: var(--gray-0);
	}

	.content {
		grid-column: 2 / 4;
	}

	.content :global(a) {
		text-decoration: 1px solid underline transparent;
		text-underline-offset: 0.25em;
		transition: text-decoration-color var(--theme-transition);
	}

	.content :global(a:hover),
	.content :global(a:focus) {
		text-decoration-color: currentColor;
	}

	@media (min-width: 50em) {
		.about {
			display: grid;
			grid-template-columns: 1fr 60% 1fr;
		}

		.about > :global(:first-child) {
			grid-column-start: 2;
		}

		section {
			display: contents;
			font-size: var(--text-lg);
		}
	}
</style>
